It is Friday evening and I am travelling home.
The U-Bahn is full, so I am standing.
I look at my phone.
Our badminton group has a chat.
Lena writes a message to everyone.
She asks: "Do you have time next week?"
Max answers immediately.
He writes: "No, I am on holiday."
Then Timo sends a photo from the sports hall.
He is still training a bit today.
Timo writes that he can play on Thursday.
I hold on with one hand.
With the other hand I type my answer.
I write: "I am playing too!"
Normally I miss my stop doing this.
I mostly keep reading and forget the time.
But today I look up in time.
The doors open and I get out quickly.
